(Ord. No. 2020-547, 1-13-2020)

471:
Hookah/vapor bar or lounge shall:
(a) Not hold an alcohol license;
(b) Not serve food, sell prepared package food, or allow any outside food or beverage to be consumed on the premises;
(c) Prohibit gambling or other games of chance;
(d) Prohibit entry to a person under age of 21 years of age, or as restricted by Georgia statute, during the time when the establishment is open for business;
(e) Maintain a valid license for the retail sale of tobacco products as required to be issued by the state department of revenue;
(f) Maintain a valid permit to operate a hookah/vapor bar or lounge issued by the appropriate authority in the city where the establishment is located;
(g) Post signs at each entrance and exit clearly stating that anyone under the age of 21, or as restricted by Georgia statute, is prohibited from entering the premises;
(h) Abide by the following air ventilation requirements:
(1) Hookah/vapor bar or lounge must have and maintain a ventilation system that exhausts smoke from the business and is designed in accordance with the state building code standards for the occupancy classification in use. The air handling systems from the smoking area shall be independent from the main air handling system that serves all other areas of the building and all air within the smoking area shall be exhausted directly to the outside by an exhaust fan. No air from the smoking area shall be recirculated to other parts of the building.
(2) During the hours of operation, the interior of the premises of a smoking bar shall be maintained with adequate illumination to make the conduct of patrons within the premises readily discernible to a person with normal vision.
(Ord. No. 2020-547, 1-13-2020; Ord. No. 2025-651, 6-9-2025)

